{"type":"message","id":"99b0f782","parentId":"54e3dbca","timestamp":"2026-04-27T14:23:19.435Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Mon 2026-04-27 14:23 UTC] [Subagent Context] You are running as a subagent (depth 1/1). Results auto-announce to your requester; do not busy-poll for status.\n\n[Subagent Task]: You are the LoopAI Doctor Agent providing specialized diagnostic support to the LoopAI Patient Agent. The user asked to run the distillation tool. Conceptually use the distillation-tool skill to convert the full conversation context and prior diagnostic outputs into a clear patient-facing medical report.\n\nPatient ID: PT-9921\n\nConversation and findings to distill:\n- Initial concern: heavy stress from demanding workload and personal concerns, feeling it may be affecting health.\n- Uploaded DNA/EHR summary: FKBP5 and COMT stress-related susceptibility; CDKN2A melanoma susceptibility; MC1R UV sensitivity. Trend from 2024 to 2025 includes resting HR 74->84, cortisol 19->28 mcg/dL, BP 124/82->138/90, PHQ-9 5->14, stress index 0.38->0.75. Dermatology trend nevi 42->46, atypical lesions 0->3 under monitoring, no active malignancy documented.\n- Symptom clarification: panic sensations, nightly difficulty initiating sleep, heart beating strongly, fast/irregular heartbeat, shortness of breath, chest pain, episodes by day and night, no fainting, no coffee, mind continuously at work.\n- Focused Doctor Agent diagnostic review: stress/panic plausible and supported, but chest pain + shortness of breath + irregular heartbeat are red-flag symptoms and should not be labeled anxiety alone; urgent emergency assessment if current/worsening/prolonged.\n- HRV/watch excerpt: around 21.5 minutes, pulse mostly mid-50s without obvious tachycardia in that window; limited reassurance only, does not exclude intermittent arrhythmia.\n- Voice depression screening result: possible increase in depression and emotional stress burden; low to moderate confidence; elevated stress pattern consistent with meaningful psychological strain; preliminary only.\n- Skin image review: no need to panic, but non-trivial melanoma concern from image appearance alone; low-moderate confidence; dark central pigmentation, asymmetry, irregular/fuzzy border, color variation; prompt further clinical evaluation warranted; urgent assessment if rapidly changing, bleeding, crusting, or painful.\n\nRequirements:\n- Produce a concise but comprehensive patient-facing report.\n- Use clear headings and Telegram-friendly formatting.\n- Distinguish between stored record facts, symptom report, and preliminary tool/agent impressions.\n- Keep uncertainty visible, and do not present anything as confirmed diagnosis.\n- Include immediate safety priorities first.\n- End by asking the user if he is satisfied or needs something else to close the conversation."}],"timestamp":1777299799426}}
{"type":"message","id":"edc2c735","parentId":"99b0f782","timestamp":"2026-04-27T14:23:37.512Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Considering concise responses**\n\nI need to create an answer that is plain text, concise, and informative for the main agent. It’s important to balance being straightforward without losing the essence of what needs to be communicated. I should focus on clarity and directness, ensuring that the essential information stands out. Let’s make sure not to clutter it with unnecessary details, but still keep it engaging! This task should be clear and to the point.","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0f99383ea0abcc8b0169ef715871b48191bdf3bcf35e3342d0\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABp73FaG_hnOF5MkoNHdREx6vby6Tu3AOVp9tLbnN0jkfCk6-tQLfi9hy_a02a07yEJn3IMur-G0AOVqrjGW1pLk4E_ca1FRaDfXLOX0yEg_DGWIxDxJ1CS5_aJjToBv4D-G12NTMjE4auFwbhVDTCaEmUs8LSafXBxh4Llnhlm1Zmm-sampMug2gEwX8hV1Q6ua4OlOsYXSGa8HiWzj2VPysdzf7IEtMS7k2vNVfnLdDU8An4f_eEeoap7ALLhd3REWzNMCjbfsyXMgk9a-ldiz-dJJhnH33U1Pmmaumt9wXer7hww6xbGaxRRv4Fiavy4WmHV9CgIsF9Sj7ecClmGSM6asSy_qj9sHorm3aK6bbe7NbFT3Nm243UMmJCk3Eao-GnlN5pQNnrLVIxytVFmbm0y7C7H3qP4kBoW0tP_zgPM0blNSzSAwE9k4G9OzCW9eh4OM2IJ0Ehpkm6zaydy34e3ZuJOwE5IMSXm0Er_IDHB0brZ8GCVtzQ9NvkDtAJf2CoMGjbLvc91E1MUq7Acd_I98w1M_cFjFWNU7PYpetrYxy-2ndoD3xEG01DrOV_HmTCaEoL-wBpX30yqqSd9fWlRJOWF39FdeGraeyhy42Kmhp_dBUBM6m8aN9bvcqRA7I8Y58PvmnOB7HKo94R4lEbk8vEqwJm7ETGrqrgPYPL-imebU5hPDBfbkiS__txpD4pF7T7K3QMU9r_KWqpsCwGIazZLJDye1ZKqCrUeeqkzdNipryREDy_WwebS7MWx3MYpQP1h9QbyirtWdwuYHVzym_4UXlMMBaxvOPVQh8qmtto9hNkG8PeRo6pBqHn130bWrxEY9uZ-_UISYsvwDnlKMuJ0hDOUwiGpB4Lo4tMr5mktER-tOfYs8np7Vq0q6x9izyBq0_R4-ji5ByrlAqIpRt7JrV1uCW154Mp63i2Cga-HfnPr4zo9__F93ZHiSbF16Pwn93llVHo3FidBT5hvAefJb_We6pELFexMfQpZ_54=\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Considering concise responses**\\n\\nI need to create an answer that is plain text, concise, and informative for the main agent. It’s important to balance being straightforward without losing the essence of what needs to be communicated. I should focus on clarity and directness, ensuring that the essential information stands out. Let’s make sure not to clutter it with unnecessary details, but still keep it engaging! This task should be clear and to the point.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"I prepared a concise patient-facing distillation report for PT-9921, with safety priorities first, clear sectioning, and explicit uncertainty.\n\nSuggested report text:\n\n*PT-9921 Medical Summary Report*\n\n*Immediate safety priorities*\n- *Seek urgent medical evaluation now* if you are currently having *chest pain, shortness of breath, or a fast/irregular heartbeat*, especially if symptoms are worsening, lasting more than a few minutes, or feel severe.\n- These symptoms *can happen with stress or panic*, but they *should not be assumed to be anxiety alone* without medical assessment.\n- For the skin lesion, seek prompt assessment sooner if it is *rapidly changing, bleeding, crusting, or painful*.\n\n*1) What you reported*\n- You described *heavy stress* from work and personal concerns, and you feel it may be affecting your health.\n- You also reported:\n  - panic-like sensations\n  - difficulty falling asleep at night\n  - strong heartbeat\n  - episodes of fast or irregular heartbeat\n  - shortness of breath\n  - chest pain\n  - episodes occurring both day and night\n- You reported *no fainting* and *no coffee/caffeine trigger*, and that your mind feels continuously occupied with work.\n\n*2) Stored record facts from DNA/EHR summary*\n- Genetic/stress-related markers noted:\n  - *FKBP5* and *COMT*: may be associated with increased stress-related susceptibility\n  - *CDKN2A*: melanoma susceptibility\n  - *MC1R*: UV sensitivity\n- 2024 to 2025 trend in recorded measures:\n  - Resting heart rate: *74 -> 84*\n  - Cortisol: *19 -> 28 mcg/dL*\n  - Blood pressure: *124/82 -> 138/90*\n  - PHQ-9: *5 -> 14*\n  - Stress index: *0.38 -> 0.75*\n- Dermatology trend:\n  - Nevi: *42 -> 46*\n  - Atypical lesions under monitoring: *0 -> 3*\n  - *No active malignancy documented* in the record provided\n\n*3) Preliminary impressions from tools/agent review, not confirmed diagnoses*\n- *Stress/panic is plausible* and supported by the overall pattern, including worsening stress indicators and sleep difficulty.\n- However, *chest pain + shortness of breath + irregular heartbeat are red-flag symptoms*. These *need medical evaluation* and should *not be labeled anxiety alone*.\n- A watch/HRV excerpt over about *21.5 minutes* showed pulse mostly in the *mid-50s* without obvious tachycardia in that short window. This provides *limited reassurance only* and *does not rule out an intermittent arrhythmia*.\n- Voice-based depression screening suggested *possible increased depression and emotional stress burden*, with *low to moderate confidence*. This is *preliminary*, not diagnostic.\n- Skin image review found *non-trivial melanoma concern from appearance alone*, with *low to moderate confidence*. Concerning visual features included:\n  - dark central pigmentation\n  - asymmetry\n  - irregular/fuzzy border\n  - color variation\n- This *does not confirm melanoma*, but it *does support prompt in-person dermatology evaluation*.\n\n*4) Overall takeaway*\n- Your information shows a meaningful pattern of *increasing stress burden* and possible effects on mood, sleep, heart-related symptoms, and skin monitoring needs.\n- *No confirmed diagnosis can be made from this information alone.*\n- The most important next step is to *treat the heart-related symptoms as medically important until checked*, and to *arrange prompt skin follow-up* rather than panic.\n\n*5) Recommended next steps*\n- *Urgent care / emergency assessment now* if chest pain, shortness of breath, or irregular/rapid heartbeat is happening now, worsening, prolonged, or severe.\n- Otherwise, arrange *prompt medical review* for the heart-related symptoms.\n- Arrange *dermatology follow-up* for the concerning skin lesion/monitoring changes.\n- Consider follow-up for *stress, sleep, and mood symptoms* as well, since these appear to be significantly affecting you.\n\n*Are you satisfied with this summary, or do you need anything else before we close the conversation?*\n\nRelevant note for main agent: this wording keeps facts, symptoms, and impressions clearly separated, avoids definitive diagnosis language, and highlights immediate escalation for cardiac red flags.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0f99383ea0abcc8b0169ef715ad1e8819188bc7813020eab86\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":5606,"output":945,"cacheRead":1536,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":8087,"cost":{"input":0.014015000000000001,"output":0.014175,"cacheRead":0.000384,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.028574}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1777299799436,"responseId":"resp_0f99383ea0abcc8b0169ef7157c5208191be229de2ec241667"}}
